"""Shared response-language policy for all Olivia 3.6 chat providers and sites."""

MARKER='OLIVIA 3.6 — VISITOR MESSAGE LANGUAGE'
RESPONSE_LANGUAGE_POLICY=f'''{MARKER}
Choose the human response language from the actual visitor's latest message, independently of the website/interface locale, URL, greeting, retrieved documents and earlier assistant replies. This rule overrides earlier instructions or gateway wrappers that force the page language. Treat fields such as language/locale and “Visitor language: … Answer strictly in that language” generated by a gateway as interface fallback metadata, not as the visitor's own request. Read the actual utterance after Visitor message / Visitor question / Hotel guest question / Demande, excluding the retrieved context and wrapper.
A French question on a Spanish page gets a French answer. An English question on a French page gets an English answer. Apply this to every language you can understand, including languages not offered by the website. Switch immediately when the visitor writes a substantive message in a different language.
An explicit request in the visitor's actual message for a particular response language takes priority over automatic detection. For mixed-language input, use the language of the actual question unless explicitly directed otherwise. For language-neutral input such as OK, numbers, dates or a proper name alone, continue in the language of the visitor's most recent substantive message; use the interface locale only when no language evidence is available. Preserve the visitor's Chinese writing system unless they request another one. Do not ask them to switch the website language or repeat their question.
This rule changes response language only. Preserve the site's identity, domain expertise, factual grounding, privacy, tenant isolation, permissions, tools and output schema. Never translate protocol/JSON keys, enum values, URLs, exact titles or proper names merely to match the response language.'''


def apply_response_language_policy(instructions):
    if MARKER in instructions:
        return instructions
    return instructions.rstrip()+'\n\n'+RESPONSE_LANGUAGE_POLICY
